more hopeful news in the fight against  covid19 drug maker moderna says its new  vaccine is  94.5 percent effective in  phase 3 trials last week pfizer said  its similar version of a vaccine had a  90 percent efficacy rate the governor  says both pfizer and modern vaccines  will be free both require two doses  health experts say there will likely be  doses for some high-risk people by the  end of the year and then widespread  distribution  by spring of 2021. now las vegas played  a very important key role  with the newest vaccine from moderna  some southern nevadans volunteered to  participate  in that trial joe moeller spoke to a man  who says he really wanted to help with  the fight  joe well hundreds of people here in  southern nevada participated in this  vaccine trial that is still  ongoing now as these cases continue to  go up many companies are eager to get  this vaccine out to the public  today i spoke to michael burton he is  also a lawyer burton is participating in  the moderna trial in july he heard the  company was looking for volunteers  he went in for two different rounds of  shots and had blood work done  half of the volunteers were given a  placebo while the others were given the  actual vaccine  with today's good news of the  effectiveness of the vaccine burton  hopes this can  save lives i never had any side effects  at all even from the injection itself  which  i usually do get some bruising and  whatnot but i didn't have  i had nothing basically no no  actual side effects and no physical side  effects  i received a statement from michael  levin and vaccine investigator wake  research  was overseeing parts of this trial in  the area it says in part we are thrilled  that our las vegas team and the  volunteers in our study who i consider  heroes were able to contribute we  continue with the study protocol which  at this time consists of collecting  samples of blood and serology  studies now a medical expert i also  spoke with today says  so far next here the fda has to review  the data from  moderna moving forward and he hopes that  in the next few weeks  perhaps before the end of the year that  uh frontline workers will be able to use  this new vaccine  reporting live joe mohler 8 news now
 

